1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,490
Most AI products begin with a chat box.

2
00:00:02,490 --> 00:00:07,632
Hallow begins with a private runtime—and a rule: intelligence before action, proof after it.

3
00:00:07,632 --> 00:00:12,613
Installation takes one terminal command on macOS, Linux, WSL, or Termux.

4
00:00:12,613 --> 00:00:15,189
Windows has its own one-line PowerShell installer.

5
00:00:15,189 --> 00:00:21,979
Hallow verifies dependencies, creates the private workspace, starts the managed service, and preserves existing data during updates.

6
00:00:21,979 --> 00:00:30,454
Before doing real work, Hallow Doctor checks what is actually ready: the runtime, private model route, memory boundary, tool policy, installed skills, and chain connection.

7
00:00:30,454 --> 00:00:31,742
Then define the mission.

8
00:00:31,742 --> 00:00:33,778
Investigate AAPL on Robinhood Chain.

9
00:00:33,778 --> 00:00:36,325
Show evidence, risk, and unknowns.

10
00:00:36,325 --> 00:00:39,185
One request activates multiple bounded tools.

11
00:00:39,185 --> 00:00:44,933
Hallow checks the network, official market data, token intelligence, and policy, then returns an inspectable answer.

12
00:00:44,933 --> 00:00:47,613
For real-world assets, a ticker is not enough.

13
00:00:47,613 --> 00:00:53,693
Hallow resolves the official deployment, checks market activity, public liquidity, holder distribution, and protocol readiness.

14
00:00:53,693 --> 00:00:59,460
It also states what the evidence cannot prove, including future sellability, ownership rights, and legal eligibility.

15
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:01,941
For memecoins, the same discipline applies.

16
00:01:01,941 --> 00:01:07,244
In this recorded snapshot, the deepest observed liquidity is only about eleven thousand dollars.

17
00:01:07,244 --> 00:01:08,607
Guardian stops for review.

18
00:01:08,607 --> 00:01:11,903
No swap, wallet, or private key is required.

19
00:01:11,903 --> 00:01:13,929
Hallow is more than one blockchain scanner.

20
00:01:13,929 --> 00:01:24,659
It provides private memory, bounded tools, reusable skills, long-running tasks, conversation gateways, traces, readiness checks, and controlled recovery—inside one installable agent operating system.

21
00:01:24,659 --> 00:01:27,054
Research still does not grant permission to move money.

22
00:01:27,054 --> 00:01:31,723
Guardian evaluates spending, reserve, slippage, asset identity, and risk policy.

23
00:01:31,723 --> 00:01:33,541
A human approves one exact plan.

24
00:01:33,541 --> 00:01:39,535
The dry run leaves a tamper-evident receipt while prompts, private memory, credentials, and wallet secrets remain excluded.

25
00:01:39,535 --> 00:01:42,556
Typical agents connect a model directly to action.

26
00:01:42,556 --> 00:01:47,187
Hallow builds a chain anyone can inspect: evidence, policy, consent, then proof.

27
00:01:47,187 --> 00:01:48,835
Install the agent you can inspect.

28
00:01:48,835 --> 00:01:50,075
Hallow Agent OS.

